1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,626
A delayed truck puts the next pickup at
risk.

2
00:00:03,706 --> 00:00:07,570
Rhode lets a dispatcher rehearse the
recovery, approve a feasible

3
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:11,449
replacement, and keep the driver and
detention evidence connected.

4
00:00:11,529 --> 00:00:13,920
This is the working synthetic rehearsal.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,822
A carrier is coordinating loads, drivers,
trucks,

6
00:00:16,902 --> 00:00:19,528
trailers, appointment windows, and duty
time.

7
00:00:19,608 --> 00:00:23,842
A dock delay changes several of those
commitments at once.

8
00:00:23,922 --> 00:00:26,861
Rhode brings that decision into one
workspace.

9
00:00:26,941 --> 00:00:30,172
The dispatcher can see the affected
assignment and

10
00:00:30,252 --> 00:00:33,332
compare a replacement before changing the
plan.

11
00:00:33,412 --> 00:00:35,920
Every demonstration shipment is explicitly
synthetic.

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,349
Here, Alex is delayed on the first trip.

13
00:00:39,429 --> 00:00:43,634
Recording the expected departure exposes
the next assignment at risk.

14
00:00:43,714 --> 00:00:47,920
The original commitment stays visible
while we prepare a recovery.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,777
We select Morgan with a different truck
and trailer.

16
00:00:51,857 --> 00:00:53,912
Rhode checks availability, equipment,

17
00:00:53,992 --> 00:00:56,491
declared duty budgets, and truck-route
travel time.

18
00:00:56,571 --> 00:00:59,377
The route comes from Valhalla using
Ontario

19
00:00:59,457 --> 00:01:02,491
road data and the supplied vehicle
dimensions.

20
00:01:02,571 --> 00:01:05,920
Missing evidence or an infeasible choice
stays visible.

21
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,856
The recovery review shows the existing
assignment, the proposed

22
00:01:09,936 --> 00:01:13,442
replacement, and the evidence used to make
the comparison.

23
00:01:13,522 --> 00:01:15,532
The dispatcher approves this revision.

24
00:01:15,612 --> 00:01:20,547
At that moment, the server checks the
current versions and availability again.

25
00:01:20,627 --> 00:01:25,144
If the driver or resource evidence
changed, approval returns a conflict.

26
00:01:25,224 --> 00:01:28,345
A successful approval updates assignments,
reservations,

27
00:01:28,425 --> 00:01:30,995
and the driver offer in one database
transaction.

28
00:01:31,075 --> 00:01:33,920
Repeated commands retain their original
idempotency key.

29
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,648
The driver receives a manifest with the
next

30
00:01:36,728 --> 00:01:39,520
action, stop instructions, and trip
context.

31
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,920
Acceptance is recorded separately from
dispatch.

32
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,912
On the Android emulator, we also tested
losing connectivity:

33
00:01:44,992 --> 00:01:48,016
acceptance stayed visibly pending,
survived a force-stop, and

34
00:01:48,096 --> 00:01:51,120
synchronized after reconnecting without
another assignment.

35
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:55,120
The native app preserves downloaded work
and encrypted sign-in state.

36
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,520
Tracking is an explicit work-session
choice.

37
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,667
Physical phone background-location testing

38
00:01:59,747 --> 00:02:01,920
and native iOS verification are still
deferred.

39
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,295
The same shipment keeps its document and
detention context.

40
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:09,420
This source PDF is stored privately,
hashed, and extracted with Gemini.

41
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:12,795
A dispatcher reviews corrections without
replacing the original extraction.

42
00:02:12,875 --> 00:02:15,045
Reviewed arrival instructions retain their
source.

43
00:02:15,125 --> 00:02:17,606
Detention uses arrival and departure
samples

44
00:02:17,686 --> 00:02:20,295
for the same stop and configured contract
terms.

45
00:02:20,375 --> 00:02:22,920
The reviewer must acknowledge the
observed-sample precision.

46
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,670
Approval creates a new invoice revision
and preserves the draft.

47
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:31,920
It does not collect a payment or turn
uncertain GPS into an exact timestamp.

48
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,804
Rhode also plans shared routes.

49
00:02:33,884 --> 00:02:36,819
These two less-than-truckload shipments
fit one selected vehicle.

50
00:02:36,899 --> 00:02:40,282
OR-Tools uses actual truck-route matrices
to order both pickups and

51
00:02:40,362 --> 00:02:43,978
deliveries while checking the supported
capacity and time constraints.

52
00:02:44,058 --> 00:02:46,616
The dispatcher reviews the assumptions
before approving.

53
00:02:46,696 --> 00:02:49,254
The driver accepts one complete manifest,

54
00:02:49,334 --> 00:02:51,891
and the app enforces its global stop
order.

55
00:02:51,971 --> 00:02:55,282
Vehicle reservations remain active until
all deliveries are complete.

56
00:02:55,362 --> 00:02:57,953
This preview discloses its synthetic
pallet-capacity allowance.

57
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,110
The importer reconciled all five supplied
workbook sheets: over fifteen

58
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:04,451
thousand source rows, including eighty-two
exact duplicate dispatch rows.

59
00:03:04,531 --> 00:03:06,610
Original rows, missing fields, historical
dates,

60
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:08,576
and normalized records retain their
lineage.

61
00:03:08,656 --> 00:03:10,295
Customer data remains isolated locally.

62
00:03:10,375 --> 00:03:13,732
The public preview uses synthetic
scenarios for missing operational inputs.

63
00:03:13,812 --> 00:03:16,932
Scenario replay has its own clock and
identical starting conditions,

64
00:03:17,012 --> 00:03:19,920
so modeled comparisons cannot overwrite
live operational time.

65
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,396
The deployed platform uses Firebase
identity, Cloud Run services,

66
00:03:23,476 --> 00:03:27,349
PostgreSQL with PostGIS, private Cloud
Storage, Cloud Tasks, and Vertex AI.

67
00:03:27,429 --> 00:03:30,020
Database tests cover overlapping
reservations, stale approvals,

68
00:03:30,097 --> 00:03:32,552
repeated commands, role boundaries, and
uncertain telemetry.

69
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:35,996
A cloud burst representing one hundred
thirty-one drivers completed

70
00:03:36,076 --> 00:03:38,987
without failed commands, but measured
about five point four

71
00:03:39,067 --> 00:03:42,206
seconds of synchronization lag at the
ninety-fifth percentile.

72
00:03:42,286 --> 00:03:45,920
That is a measured limit, not a two-second
service guarantee.

73
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,720
Rhode connects recovery decisions to
execution and evidence.

74
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,050
The next step is physical-device
validation and

75
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:53,270
carrier evaluation of the complete
workflow.

76
00:03:53,350 --> 00:03:56,948
Open the preview to rehearse a recovery,
inspect the assumptions,

77
00:03:57,028 --> 00:03:59,920
and follow the approved change through to
the driver.
